entry {
  full_url {
    value: "http://hl7.org/fhir/ValueSet/v3-ActClassSupply"
  }
  resource {
    value_set {
      id {
        value: "v3-ActClassSupply"
      }
      meta {
        last_updated {
          value_us: 1572560963356000
          timezone: "+11:00"
          precision: MILLISECOND
        }
        profile {
          value: "http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/shareablevalueset"
        }
      }
      text {
        status {
          value: GENERATED
        }
        div {
          value: "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><h2>V3 Value SetActClassSupply</h2><div><p>Supply orders and deliveries are simple Acts that focus on the delivered product. The product is associated with the Supply Act via Participation.typeCode=&quot;product&quot;. With general Supply Acts, the precise identification of the Material (manufacturer, serial numbers, etc.) is important.  Most of the detailed information about the Supply should be represented using the Material class.  If delivery needs to be scheduled, tracked, and billed separately, one can associate a Transportation Act with the Supply Act.  Pharmacy dispense services are represented as Supply Acts, associated with a SubstanceAdministration  Act. The SubstanceAdministration class represents the administration of medication, while dispensing is supply.</p>\n</div><p>This value set includes codes from the following code systems:</p><ul><li>Include codes from <a href=\"../../v3/ActClass/cs.html\"><code>http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActClass</code></a> where concept  is-a  <a href=\"../../v3/ActClass/cs.html#v3-ActClass-SPLY\">SPLY</a></li></ul></div>"
        }
      }
      extension {
        url {
          value: "http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/structuredefinition-standards-status"
        }
        value {
          code {
            value: "external"
          }
        }
      }
      extension {
        url {
          value: "http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/structuredefinition-fmm"
        }
        value {
          integer {
          }
        }
      }
      url {
        value: "http://terminology.hl7.org/ValueSet/v3-ActClassSupply"
      }
      identifier {
        system {
          value: "urn:ietf:rfc:3986"
        }
        value {
          value: "urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.1.11.11535"
        }
      }
      version {
        value: "2014-03-26"
      }
      name {
        value: "v3.ActClassSupply"
      }
      title {
        value: "V3 Value SetActClassSupply"
      }
      status {
        value: ACTIVE
      }
      experimental {
      }
      publisher {
        value: "HL7 v3"
      }
      contact {
        telecom {
          system {
            value: URL
          }
          value {
            value: "http://www.hl7.org"
          }
        }
      }
      description {
        value: " Supply orders and deliveries are simple Acts that focus on the delivered product. The product is associated with the Supply Act via Participation.typeCode=\"product\". With general Supply Acts, the precise identification of the Material (manufacturer, serial numbers, etc.) is important.  Most of the detailed information about the Supply should be represented using the Material class.  If delivery needs to be scheduled, tracked, and billed separately, one can associate a Transportation Act with the Supply Act.  Pharmacy dispense services are represented as Supply Acts, associated with a SubstanceAdministration  Act. The SubstanceAdministration class represents the administration of medication, while dispensing is supply."
      }
      immutable {
        value: true
      }
      compose {
        include {
          system {
            value: "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActClass"
          }
          filter {
            property {
              value: "concept"
            }
            op {
              value: IS_A
            }
            value {
              value: "SPLY"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
entry {
  full_url {
    value: "http://hl7.org/fhir/ValueSet/v3-HL7ContextConductionStyle"
  }
  resource {
    value_set {
      id {
        value: "v3-HL7ContextConductionStyle"
      }
      meta {
        last_updated {
          value_us: 1533996000000000
          timezone: "+10:00"
          precision: MILLISECOND
        }
        profile {
          value: "http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/shareablevalueset"
        }
      }
      text {
        status {
          value: GENERATED
        }
        div {
          value: "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p>Release Date: 2018-08-12</p>\r\n<table class=\"grid\">\r\n <tr><td><b>Level</b></td><td><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr>\r\n <tr><td>1</td><td>C<a name=\"v3-HL7ContextConductionStyle-C\"> </a></td><td>conduction-indicator-based</td><td>\n                        \n                           Definition: Context conduction is defined using the contextConductionCode and contextConductionInd attributes on ActRelationship and Participation.<br/>\r\n\n                        \n                           UsageNotes: This approach is deprecated as of March, 2010.<br/>\r\n\n                     </td></tr>\r\n <tr><td>1</td><td>I<a name=\"v3-HL7ContextConductionStyle-I\"> </a></td><td>inferred</td><td>\n                        \n                           Definition: Context conduction is not explicitly defined.  The recipient of an instance must infer conduction based on the semantics of the model and what is deemed &quot;reasonable&quot;.<br/>\r\n\n                        \n                           UsageNotes: Because this approach can lead to variation in instance interpretation, its use is discouraged.<br/>\r\n\n                     </td></tr>\r\n <tr><td>1</td><td>V<a name=\"v3-HL7ContextConductionStyle-V\"> </a></td><td>vocabulary-based</td><td>\n                        \n                           Definition: Context conduction is defined using the ActRelationship.blockedContextActRelationshipType and blockedContextParticipationType attributes and the &quot;conductible&quot; property on the ActRelationshipType and ParticipationType code systems.<br/>\r\n\n                     </td></tr>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>"
        }
      }
      extension {
        url {
          value: "http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/structuredefinition-standards-status"
        }
        value {
          code {
            value: "external"
          }
        }
      }
      extension {
        url {
          value: "http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/structuredefinition-fmm"
        }
        value {
          integer {
          }
        }
      }
      extension {
        url {
          value: "http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/structuredefinition-wg"
        }
        value {
          code {
            value: "vocab"
          }
        }
      }
      url {
        value: "http://terminology.hl7.org/ValueSet/v3-HL7ContextConductionStyle"
      }
      identifier {
        system {
          value: "urn:ietf:rfc:3986"
        }
        value {
          value: "urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.1.11.20380"
        }
      }
      version {
        value: "2018-08-12"
      }
      name {
        value: "v3.HL7ContextConductionStyle"
      }
      title {
        value: "v3 Code System HL7ContextConductionStyle"
      }
      status {
        value: ACTIVE
      }
      experimental {
      }
      date {
        value_us: 1533996000000000
        timezone: "Australia/Sydney"
        precision: DAY
      }
      publisher {
        value: "HL7, Inc"
      }
      contact {
        telecom {
          system {
            value: URL
          }
          value {
            value: "http://hl7.org"
          }
        }
      }
      description {
        value: "The styles of context conduction usable by relationships within a static model derived from tyhe HL7 Reference Information Model."
      }
      immutable {
        value: true
      }
      compose {
        include {
          system {
            value: "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-HL7ContextConductionStyle"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
